# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Orbit — Marketplace lead-capture webhook config
# Copy the relevant line(s) into your main .env (do NOT commit real keys).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shared secret that inbound marketplace webhooks must send in the
# `x-orbit-key` request header.
#
#   • If SET:   POST /api/marketplace/<source> requires a matching
#               `x-orbit-key` header (401 otherwise). The Integrations
#               console shows "Configured".
#   • If UNSET: the webhook runs in dev mode — it accepts unauthenticated
#               requests and returns a `note` saying so. The console shows
#               "Dev mode". Fine for local testing; DO NOT ship to prod unset.
#
# Generate a strong value, e.g.:  openssl rand -hex 32
MARKETPLACE_WEBHOOK_KEY=

# Notes:
#  • Paste the webhook URL shown on /integrations into each seller panel
#    (IndiaMART Lead Manager CRM/Push API, JustDial lead webhook,
#     TradeIndia inquiry API, or your website form action).
#  • DEMO tenant resolution: the webhook attaches leads to the first tenant
#    in the DB. In production, map this key (or a per-source key) to a
#    specific tenant instead — see app/api/marketplace/[source]/route.ts.
